From 3bcd02aae62038068eb7f54aa3066aabc1ee2fe1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Magnus Reimann <magnus.reimann@mailbox.org>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:27:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH gnumach 10/22] tests: add an SMP stress test

No test runs anything on more than one processor: the APs start in
their own processor set, and the test tasks stay in the default one,
so with -smp 2 the second processor only runs its idle thread.

Add test-smp, which moves all processors to the default processor set
with processor_assign, then runs several threads doing VM and IPC
operations on the task's shared map and port space, and checks that
they did run on more than one processor.

* tests/test-smp.c: New file.
* tests/user-qemu.mk (USER_TESTS): Add tests/test-smp.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tests/test-smp.c   | 173 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 tests/user-qemu.mk |   1 +
 2 files changed, 174 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 tests/test-smp.c

diff --git a/tests/test-smp.c b/tests/test-smp.c
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..107ac75d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/test-smp.c
@@ -0,0 +1,173 @@
